Stage042 source-built C environment. Boot: shell> enter start - dev . All target code generation occurs in the guest.
Clean source-only entry: shell> batch bootplan . Trusted unchanged041 kernel/assembler:21012 bytes, SHA256 b5392072bdcfb35971c00392d5bf153f593630864615b5349f68813c2b416aa8. Pre-seed legacy filenames are alphanumeric,1..12 bytes; dotted C filenames are supported only after mounting the new filesystem. Initial contains ONLY21 declared source/data files listed in initial, no executable cache.
Live canonical components: layout; word32/lz/fs42/native42/codesize; cc.c; runtime/io42; shellcore/process/dev.c; start.c. Original pinned alpha/beta/extra5/arg/header bytes are unchanged. Preserved extra2/extra4/console/stage/guard/forge are historical sources, NOT the live interface authority.
Limits:128 filenames of1..47 bytes;196608 bytes/file; source131072; preprocessing196596; aligned code4..131064. Logical filesystem1572864 bytes including9216 metadata. Durable data additionally must fit851960 LZ bytes in a private851968-byte container. Incompressible aggregates may fail before RAM is full. No partial stream is published; failed commit retains the old disk, with unsaved working-image changes. Check errors.
Memory/capacities derive from layout: compiler41100000, shell41140000, output41180000, USER411c0000, APP41200000, PP41240000, loader41280000, editor412c0000; filesystem41340000..414c0000; snapshot41500000; input41600000; transfer41700000; pipes41800000/41840000; scratch41940000..41ac0000; plan41b20000; SHA41c00000; tests41d00000..41ec0000; immutable boot41f00000. Legacy staging40b00000/compiler40150000 are bootstrap-private.
Legacy transport cache+4096 MUST equal32768 for24 slots. Zero selects16x8192 and caused the old failed cold export. export.c writes it explicitly. New container40409400..404d9400 is below transport end404e0400. Legacy batch control41b00000/argv41b10000 are reserved; plan uses41b20000. PACKMAGIC/length/LZ/checksum are validated. fsmount also verifies/migrates an older raw image in RAM; migrate.c documents explicit publication.
Executable: u32le code length then code; optional EXEZ wraps LZ of that same file. native validates in LOADBUF before publishing. ONE filename per executable; no parts, required packing, or project-source archiving. Red is deliberately saved uncompressed above64KiB.
Commands: edit FILE; build SOURCE; save EXECUTABLE; load EXECUTABLE; exec argv0 [args]; SOURCE [args]; @EXECUTABLE [args]; list; show; check; copy OLD NEW; replace FILE OLD NEW; remove; extract ARCHIVE MEMBER; plan FILE; quit. Build/load failure preserves USER/compiler. install explicitly replaces the compiler; running applications does not.
Editor: p; i N text; r N text; d N; w durably saves; q discards unsaved changes. Shell quotes work; no globbing/variables/escapes. Whitespace-separated < > >> 2> and pipes, max8 stages,196608 bytes/pipe. Upstream tools and ordinary programs use identical descriptors and return/exit paths.
red.c is46219 bytes and performs2000 real increments; blue.c is independent and exits7. binary.c input.bin 40000 generates data; @cat input.bin | binary.c | @cat > output.bin transforms every byte, including NUL/EOT. Imported output data alone is NOT a test: rebuild42 regenerates both streams.
Normal source rebuild: plan rebuild42 . It stops at the first error, retains source/data and compares successive compiler generations. Inventory files record exact initial inputs, archive members, trusted boot and generated output hashes. Earlier successful writes are not rolled back on a later plan failure.
Destructive clean/recovery: export.c initial yes verifies and writes a newly zeroed legacy source/data disk, then never returns. Stop/reboot, batch bootplan. This retains recorded inputs, NOT later unrecorded edits: update work with archive.c first if needed. Normal edit/build/save/reboot needs no archives, deletion, reset or export.
Bootstrap: assemble new1; compile extra1,extra3,raw,precc,bridge,seed. Seed imports/verifies every input, unpacks declared source/data archives, builds/compares three cc generations, builds dev/start, publishes only checked images, then runs rebuild42. No saved compiler/tool is used by this entry.
Archive encoding: u8 name length,u16le data length,name,data; terminal zero. Generic LZ: u32le decoded length, literal tag0..127 means tag+1 bytes; match tag128..255 means tag-128+3 bytes plus u16le backward distance. bundle/aux/work contain source and declared data only. @sha -z inventories compressed archive members; -a inventories raw archives.
Inherited C subset, not ISO C:128 functions,32 locals,16 globals,4 arguments; no general structs/typedefs/prototypes/local arrays/variadics/division/bitwise or <=/>=. Object macros and conditional includes, no function macros/#if. bits supplies generic AArch64 bit operations for SHA/fixtures.
Trusted single-process raw-memory environment, not POSIX isolation/concurrency. No timeout or physical power-loss transaction guarantee. Low-level fsput edits RAM; fscommit publishes, ordinary descriptors/editor saves call it. test.c/bounds.c/ppbound.c/physical.c are ordinary C fixtures for count/file/aggregate/source/code/PP/overlap/physical-capacity errors and preservation.
